I updated the game with several bug fixes and ‘quality of life’ improvements.

The main contents include:
*A bug fix for the 1 hp error in the final battle;
*Improvements in the Badge acquisition system inside the Trophy Room. Now you will not see badges you already own in the mainframe that is used to recover new badges;
*A few minor map bugfixes;
*Improvements in all language files;
*Improvements in badge items which are now limit to one of each kind.

Thank you for playing our game and writing to us! Your comments and ratings are ver appreciated.

Sincerely,
BoneCollectors.

Improvements:
*DINOdex menu rebuilt with new artwork and design. It looks more appealing and cute now;
*Options menu redesigned;
*Manual screen redesigned;

Hotfix:
*Tropeognathus description;
*Mesoeucrocodylian description;
*Axelrhodichthys typo;
*Trophy Room badge terminal fixed for the Late Cretaceous and early Paleozoic badges;

We are going to stay a while without any updates because we will be on an expedition on a remote jungle area. Wish us luck!

Bye!

Hotfix for the bugs listed below:

*Font glitches are finally over (forever);
*Manual bug for the DINOdex text in English and Korean;
*I fixed how the sleepy mushroom bait affects the animals;
*I removed the armor version cyberhelmet and exchanged it for the keyitem version;
*Removed the autosave point after the cutscene in the Water Station to avoid freezing screens when players get a game over.

Improvements:

*Item menu rewritten;
*Shop menu rewritten;
*Minor improvements in all languages;
*Currency symbol updated;
*I simplified the Options menu;

We released a new patch containing a new sidequest scene and a hotfix for several bugs reported by the community in these past weeks:

*Improvements in JAPANESE language;
*I added an attempt to fix the font glitches;
*I improved some battle backgrounds;
*I fixed the 'line.match' frozen screens that some players were finding when battling on rainy days.

As for the sidequest, go to the southern islet in Part 5. :)

Ah! I also changed the 'small ornithopod' spawining on the Early Cretaceous maps to Tietasaura since a similar fossil species was recently described from Brazil.

Keep sending me the forum messages! They are very relevant!

Sincerely,
BC.

